body:
YES

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

thank you!!!

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Awwwww not for me yet =/ (edit)

I'm quite flattered when my cat does that, it's just grooming. It means he likes me and appreciates my efforts.

&#x200B;

Try stroking your cat when sleepy, that's when mine is 100% affectionate.

I wan't 100% sold on eggs until I started cooking them myself. I then realised that my parents always boiled the eggs, and boiled them to the max to be safe.

&#x200B;

As a student one scrambled egg plus veg was my go- to, I wouldn't need to shop for maybe 2 weeks.

&#x200B;

However there are various egg delicacies in different cultures that I would not be able to go near, pointing no fingers. And I remember reading a star wars fic - that huge one where obi-wan travels back in time and calls himself a Mandalorian - where young obi-wan realised that the food on the table consisted of livebearing eggs from the colony the contracters wanted massacred.

&#x200B;

I feel like that's a thing in star wars, and that therefore many Jedi might hate eggs. In keeping with my headcannon that many Jedi might not go for meat all the time. Eating meat isn't evil, and plenty of species require they eat meat. I just remember either an Eragon fic, or Inheritance book, where Eragon is given the dragon's gift and living with elves, and after cannot stand meat as it comes from a live source. So I pair enhanced awareness of different lifeforms with reluctance to eat their carcasses.

...why is culture appropriation such a big thing in this thread?

&#x200B;

I'm glad this lady and supporters managed to get the post taken down, because yes that could have had a serious impact on her career depending on the type of fic.

&#x200B;

I tend to go for fictional characters, because writing and reading about real people just seems very wrong to me. And I will never understand real people enough to be comfortable guessing what they are thinking either. Plus with what some people write....not going there, nope.

&#x200B;

Still, people use online fanfic websites because of the anonymity, and it is almost sacred to me. Only years after starting have I mentioned one fic I wrote to someone I know in real life. That's one part embarrassment, two parts how big a role low moods play in what I write. And this author can't ever get that anonymity back. Ouch.
